{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>ונירם.</b> The words of Moses, and the mem is a sign of 'the king of Sihon and his hosts,' and it has two interpretations. The first: from the root ניר, and the word ונירם is drawn by itself and another after it, like והנבואה עודד הנביא. And so it is: ונירם אבד — 'their nîr is lost,' namely the ניר of Heshbon, and the word ונירם is like 'in the midst of the tents of the rechecha' — and so it is: their nîr, which is the nîr of Heshbon, is lost. The second interpretation: that the word ונירם is from the root ירה, like 'יור which I shot,' and the meaning is: when we shot them, Heshbon was lost." "<b>ונשים.</b> Of the doubled stems, and the ḥiriq in place of small qamatz, like 'ויסב Elohim את העם.' And Rabbi Moses the Priest said that the dagesh is for the loss of the alef, like 'alef from before מבהמות ארץ,' from the root 'תאשם שומרון.' And some say that Heshbon was the city of Sihon forever, and the meaning of 'בואו חשבון' is the words of the speakers to the Moabites coming into captivity at Heshbon: 'for fire went out from Heshbon' — a parable for the camps of Sihon; and when we shot them, the words of the speakers in the Moabites' tongue: we thought that Heshbon would be lost, and the whole land would become a desolation as far as Nophah. Or they are the words of Moses the darshan."], :book :numbers, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:18:48.869795747Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}